# Snyk (https://snyk.io) policy file.
#
# Ignore policy for Snyk Code (SAST) findings. Each already has a real,
# verified code-level mitigation; see the inline `deepcode ignore` comment at
# each site for the full rationale.
#
# Ignore-duration policy: time-limited to 30 days and re-reviewed, EXCEPT
# findings determined to be permanent false positives (a mitigation Snyk's
# engine structurally cannot model, where the "fix" would break functionality),
# which carry no expiry.
#
# NOTE: org e6qu uses platform-managed Consistent Ignores, so this file is not
# honored by the local `snyk code test` CLI. It serves as in-repo documentation
# and as the source of truth if policy-as-code is enabled; the same
# determinations/expiries are mirrored in the Snyk UI/API ignores.
version: v1.25.0
ignore:
  # PERMANENT false positive — no expiry.
  # Snyk's go/XSS only credits stdlib HTML-escaping as a sanitizer, which can
  # never apply to a markdown->HTML rendering endpoint. Output is allowlist-
  # sanitized by bluemonday (strips javascript:/data: URLs, event handlers, and
  # disallowed elements) — the same approach GitHub uses. Verified by
  # TestMarkdownSanitizesDangerousSchemes. The engine limitation is permanent.
  go/XSS:
    - internal/server/gh_markdown.go:
        reason: >-
          Permanent false positive. Rendered markdown is allowlist-sanitized by
          bluemonday; Snyk's go/XSS only recognizes stdlib HTML-escaping, which
          would defeat markdown rendering. Verified by
          TestMarkdownSanitizesDangerousSchemes.

  # PERMANENT false positive — no expiry.
  # Build-time asset-vendoring tool. The request target is a compile-time
  # constant (twemojiTarballURL), validated https/host and SHA-256 pinned; it is
  # never derived from input, environment, or a redirect. There is nothing to
  # sanitize, so the finding is permanently spurious.
  go/Ssrf:
    - internal/emojigen/main.go:
        reason: >-
          Permanent false positive. Compile-time-constant, SHA-256-pinned URL in
          a build-time tool; never input-derived. Snyk flags the Get purely for
          being reachable from a CLI flag.

  # ACCEPTED RISK, not a false positive — TIME-LIMITED to 30 days, re-review by
  # 2026-09-03. InsecureSkipVerify genuinely relaxes CA/hostname verification;
  # it is the opt-in webhook insecure_ssl=1 feature (GitHub parity) and cannot
  # exist without the flag. Hardened with a TLS 1.2 floor and a VerifyConnection
  # that rejects absent/expired certs, but residual MITM exposure remains when
  # an operator opts in. Re-review whether the feature should stay / be hardened
  # further.
  go/TooPermissiveTrustManager:
    - internal/server/webhooks.go:
        reason: >-
          Accepted risk (opt-in webhook insecure_ssl=1 feature, GitHub parity),
          not a false positive. Hardened with TLS 1.2 floor + expiry-checking
          VerifyConnection. Time-limited; re-review whether to keep or further
          harden the feature.
        expires: 2026-09-03T00:00:00.000Z
